I believe it would be possible to compile nethack under msdos using
power C provided a nethack.prj file could be made.
What the nethack.prj file would need to have inside it would be each program name on a line
by itself.  So if there was a program called armor.c and an
include file called armor.h in the source, and armor.c included armor.h
the only line for this that would be in the nethack.prj file would be:
armor <cr>.  I would like to know the files needed to compile in order of
compilation so I can try this.
Power C is very close to microsoft C and is heavily into ansi conventions.
If you can't make this kind of file but can send me a message with the files
in it or at least their order I'll be able to roll my own nethack.prj file
and send it back to you.

